Chapter 1
Zhen Shi-yin encounters the Spiritual Jade in a dream;
Jia Yu-cun, in straitened circumstances, cherishes a woman of the inner rooms

Chapter 2
Jia Min dies in Yangzhou;
Leng Zi-xing describes the Rong mansion

Chapter 3
Jia Yu-cun is restored to office in Jinling;
Lin Dai-yu is taken into the Rong mansion

Grandmother Jia laughed. ‘Changing out of your clothes before you’ve even met our visitor! Go and greet your cousin.’
Bao-yu had already noticed the additional girl and guessed that she was his Aunt Lin’s daughter. He hurried over and bowed. When they had exchanged greetings and sat down again, he studied her features. She was unlike all the others:
Two mist-veiled brows, drawn together, yet not quite frowning;
Two dew-filled eyes, seeming glad, yet not quite glad.
Sorrow shaped the two dimples in her cheeks;
Illness lent its charm to all her slender body.
Her tears glimmered, drop by drop;
Her breath came in faint little gasps.
At rest, a lovely flower reflected in water;
In motion, a frail willow held by the wind.
Her heart had one opening more than Bi Gan’s;
Her frailty surpassed Xi Shi’s by three degrees.
After looking at her, Bao-yu said with a smile, ‘I have met this cousin before.’

Chapter 4
An ill-fated girl meets an ill-fated young man;
The Gourd Temple monk muddles a muddled case

Chapter 5
A visit to the Land of Illusion offers guidance through the Twelve Beauties;
Over immortal wine, songs unfold the Dream of the Red Chamber

[Kin Torn Apart]
A sail in wind and rain, a journey of three thousand li;
home and kin, all left behind.
Fearing tears will harm their declining years,
I tell my parents, ‘Do not worry about your child.
Hardship and advancement have always had their appointed course;
can meeting and parting be without their destined ties?
From now on we shall live in separate places;
let each keep safe and well.

Those in office, their family estates decline;
the wealthy and honoured, their gold and silver scattered.
Those who have shown kindness escape from death;
the heartless receive their plain reward.
Those owing life have paid with life;
those owing tears have exhausted them.
Wrong repaying wrong is no light matter;
partings and reunions were all ordained before.
To learn why life is short, ask of a former life;
even wealth and honour in old age are truly a lucky escape.
Those who see through it retreat into the Buddhist gate;
the deluded throw their lives away for nothing.
Like birds returning to the woods when all the food is gone,
they leave the great earth white and bare,
clean at last!

Chapter 6
Jia Bao-yu first tastes the love of cloud and rain;
Grannie Liu makes her first visit to the Rong mansion

Chapter 7
Palace flowers are delivered while Jia Lian dallies with Xi-feng;
At a feast in the Ning mansion Bao-yu meets Qin Zhong

Chapter 8
Comparing the Spiritual Jade, Oriole lets slip a hint;
Visiting Bao-chai, Dai-yu half betrays her jealousy

Chapter 9
Drawn by affection, two friends enter the family school;
Roused by suspicion, unruly boys turn the classroom upside down

Chapter 10
The widow Jin swallows an insult for the sake of gain;
Doctor Zhang examines an illness and traces its cause
